Data sources (attribution required when displaying or distributing):
- Maps, elevation (swissALTI3D), swissTLM3D hiking trails: © swisstopo
  (Federal Office of Topography swisstopo, free geodata / OGD terms)
- Routing network, huts and accommodation: © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL)
- Public transport stops: Federal Office of Transport BAV (list of stops, OGD)
- Public transport: opentransportdata.swiss
- The official hiking routes (national, regional, local, barrier-free):
  Wanderland Schweiz, ASTRA / SchweizMobil (ch.astra.wanderland,
  opendata.swiss, open use, source required); named on every route's page
- Reference stages for calibration (swiss/testdata/reference_stages.json):
  Wanderland Schweiz, ASTRA / SchweizMobil (opendata.swiss, open use, source
  required)

Algorithms:
- Swiss hiking time: SchweizMobil variant of the Schweizer Wanderwege formula,
  as published in geoadmin/mf-geoadmin3 (src/components/profile/ProfileService.js).
  Re-implemented in Go (swiss/hikingtime).

Code derived from third-party projects is listed below with its license.
- HEIC photos are decoded with github.com/gen2brain/heic (MIT), which embeds
  the Rust heic decoder (github.com/imazen/heic, AGPL-3.0-only) compiled to
  WebAssembly.
- api/internal/imports/komoot.go: use of Komoot's unofficial API (login, tour
  list, tour coordinates) follows the Komoot plugin of wanderer
  (github.com/open-wanderer/wanderer, plugins/komoot), AGPL-3.0.
  Re-implemented in Go for Alvyo on 2026-09-23.
